  "reconstructionNotes": "Square framed plot, x-axis 'x (m)' ticks -2..4, y-axis 'y (m)' ticks -2..2. Render a quiver grid of dark-blue arrows whose length scales with the dipole field magnitude (long near (0,0) and (2,0), shrinking to tiny dots at the frame edges); arrows radiate outward from (0,0) and converge inward on (2,0), with intermediate directions in between. In field-line mode, draw smooth continuous curves leaving the + charge at (0,0) and terminating on the - charge at (2,0), plus a few lines escaping to the frame edges. On hover, enlarge the nearest arrow, show a '|E| = ...' readout, and overlay two contribution vectors (orange outward from (0,0), green inward toward (2,0)) whose tip-to-tail sum equals the resultant. Keep arrow color a single dark blue; use distinct orange/green only for the hover decomposition so superposition reads instantly."
